From 72414d8487121ad29703b096250039067564747f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James Clancey <james.clancey@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 06:07:55 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Phase 4: wire open_duck_anim animation engine into the
 on-robot runtime
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds the runtime-side integration of the already-tested open_duck_anim core
(three-layer Engine, measured head safety envelope, clip IO, limiters) into
the 50 Hz control loop, with the safety machinery the core deliberately omits.

New package mini_bdx_runtime/anim/:
* fsm.py      - ModeFSM: BOOT/DISARMED -> ARMING -> {DOCK_DEMO,STAND,WALK},
                latched FAULT with explicit operator reset. ARMING ramps from
                the measured pose to init_pos; quantitative transition guards
                (joint pos error, joint vel, IMU tilt, contact, dwell/timeout,
                hysteresis).
* safety.py   - Minimum safety set: controlled clip abort (blend-back over
                T_alpha), deadman/e-stop -> latched FAULT, deadline + stale-
                command watchdogs, ThermalManager (duty-cycle model; HWI has
                no temp/current API). Fault action defaults to CONTROLLED_HOLD;
                thermal/overload forces TORQUE_OFF.
* controller.py - AnimationController: evaluates the Engine EXACTLY once per
                tick from one monotonic clock, routes head output through the
                additive path + derated envelope, enforces the mode x channel
                capability matrix, applies the final 14-DOF bus velocity clip.
                make_head_engine() is the single source of truth for the head
                envelope + physical joint limits.
* hardware.py - RobotInterface ABC + MockRobot so the FSM/safety are testable
                with no robot attached.
* real_robot.py - lazy-import on-robot adapter (tilt-from-accel estimate).

scripts/v2_rl_walk_mujoco.py:
* Optional --head_animation overlay: Engine evaluated once per tick from the
  loop clock, envelope-clamped head offsets routed into last_commands[3:7] so
  they flow through the KEPT deployed additive head path; antennas/sounds/
  projector driven from the engine show track; legs never touched.
* Re-enabled the max_motor_velocity (5.24 rad/s) clip on the FINAL bus targets
  (after the additive head), per plan §6.5.

scripts/dock_demo.py: no-RL DOCK_DEMO entry point that plays a .duckanim clip
library (legs held at init_pos, head/antennas/eyes animated at 50 Hz).

clips/idle_alive.duckanim (+ generator): authored "alive" idle head loop,
within the derated envelope.

tests/: 49 tests (FSM transitions/guards/latched-fault/arming ramp, abort/
blend-back, watchdogs, thermal, capability matrix, additive head, final clip,
shared engine factory).

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
